89s|a|Having the color of the clear sky, or a hue resembling it, whether lighter or darker; as, the deep, blue sea; as blue as a sapphire; blue violets. ; Pale, without redness or glare, -- said of a flame; hence, of the color of burning brimstone, betokening the presence of ghosts or devils; as, the candle burns blue; the air was blue with oaths. ; Low in spirits; melancholy; as, to feel blue. ; Suited to produce low spirits; gloomy in prospect; as, thongs looked blue. ; Severe or over strict in morals; gloom; as, blue and sour religionists; suiting one who is over strict in morals; inculcating an impracticable, severe, or gloomy mortality; as, blue laws. ; Literary; -- applied to women; -- an abbreviation of bluestocking.	j:1v19,105,2;hsq,86,2;29om,83,2;vuw,83,4;1y6i,80,3;1361,79,2;qaf,76,3;259w,76,3;1fsr,74,5;1hcy,68,9;27bj,68,4;20zl,68,2;22ed,65,2;1w3w,64,2;dvv,63,6~1649,20,80;20qx,41,44;15mc,18,26;lyz,36,24;crp,32,23;1v6i,32,22;dvr,9,22;wj2,29,14;4os,18,13;1x89,20,12;1o8e,44,12;22pi,37,12;22fg,54,10;23jm,33,10;8k5,4,10	e:1l1k,36,2;24m4,18,4;1sf0,16,1~24m4,18,4;1l1k,36,2;1sf0,16,1
